Droppen @VERSION@ for Linux, as an AppImage

Droppen is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
only (AGPL-3.0-only): usr/lib/Droppen/LICENSE. Its source code is at
https://github.com/getdroppen/droppen; this AppImage is from its release
https://github.com/getdroppen/droppen/releases/tag/v@VERSION@
usr/lib/Droppen/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES lists the third-party software built into
Droppen and into the server it carries. This AppImage also carries:

1. Libraries of Ubuntu 22.04 (GTK, WebKitGTK, GLib, GStreamer's core and what
   they need) and their data, from Ubuntu's packages, as Ubuntu built them but
   for the run path linuxdeploy set in each library. Each package's copyright
   and licence terms are in usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright, and the licence
   texts those name in usr/share/common-licenses/. Which file comes from which
   package, in which version, is in LIBRARIES-<arch>.txt on the release above.

2. The AppImage runtime, the program at the head of this file: type2-runtime,
   release 20251108 (https://github.com/AppImage/type2-runtime), under the MIT
   License, with code of libfuse 3.15.0 (GNU Lesser General Public License,
   version 2.1: usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.1) and squashfuse 0.5.2, and
   of Alpine Linux 3.21's musl libc, libzstd, zlib and mimalloc, linked in,
   each under its terms below.

3. AppRun (AppRun.wrapped), from AppImageKit, and the hook
   apprun-hooks/linuxdeploy-plugin-gtk.sh, which linuxdeploy-plugin-gtk wrote,
   each under the MIT License below.

The source code is on the same release as this AppImage, in
Droppen-@VERSION@-linux-sources.tar: the Ubuntu source package of every
package LIBRARIES-<arch>.txt names, in the very version this AppImage carries,
and the runtime's, type2-runtime at the commit of its release 20251108 with
the libfuse 3.15.0 and squashfuse 0.5.2 releases its build compiles in.

